---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout lang="en" title="Terms of Use | BrewMind" description="Terms of use for the BrewMind app and the account that comes with it.">
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-28 pb-20 px-6">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>

      <p>
        This is a translation for your convenience. The German version is the binding one:
        <a href="/terms/">Nutzungsbedingungen</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Provider and scope</h2>
      <p>
        The provider of the BrewMind app is Tegrovio, Dominik Palzer, Sterntalerweg 65,
        40235 Düsseldorf, email: <a href="mailto:hello@brewmind.app">hello@brewmind.app</a>
        (hereinafter “I”).
      </p>
      <p>
        These terms apply to the use of the BrewMind app on iPhone and Android and to the
        account that comes with it. When you sign in to the app, a contract of use is concluded
        on these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What BrewMind is</h2>
      <p>
        BrewMind helps with dialing in espresso: the app records shots, remembers the settings
        for each bean and suggests what you can change for the next shot. You can pair a
        Bluetooth scale; the app also works without one.
      </p>
      <p>
        The app's suggestions are pointers for preparing coffee. They do not replace the
        operating manual of your machine or grinder. You yourself are responsible for the safe
        handling of hot water, steam and pressure.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Minimum age</h2>
      <p>
        You may use BrewMind if you are at least 18&nbsp;years old. No age verification takes
        place. If I learn that an account belongs to a younger person, I delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Account</h2>
      <p>
        You need an account to use the app. You sign in with Apple or with Google; there is no
        separate password for BrewMind. You yourself are responsible for the security of your
        Apple or Google account.
      </p>
      <p>
        The account backs up your shots, beans and equipment so that you can restore them on a
        new device after signing in. What is processed in doing so is set out in the
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        An account belongs to one person. Do not pass on the access. If you want to use BrewMind
        together with others, that is what the household is for.
      </p>

      <h3>Household</h3>
      <p>
        You can link your account with the accounts of up to five other people to form a
        household. Each person needs their own account. In the household you share beans,
        equipment and shots; what the others see of you in doing so is set out in the
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Inviting.</strong> You invite with a link or code that is valid for
          48&nbsp;hours and for one person. Anyone who has it and is signed in to the app can
          join the household without further confirmation. Pass an invitation on only to the
          person you want to invite, and do not invite anyone who is younger than 18&nbsp;years.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Equal rights.</strong> All people in the household have the same rights. Each
          can invite further people, leave the household and remove other people from the
          household. There is no person with special rights.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Joining.</strong> When you join, your beans, equipment and shots move into the
          household. This cannot be undone.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Leaving.</strong> Anyone who leaves the household or is removed receives a
          copy of everything that was in the household up to that point, including the shots of
          the others. What you have shared in the household therefore cannot be retrieved in the
          app. Your statutory rights, in particular under the GDPR (DSGVO, the EU General Data
          Protection Regulation), remain unaffected.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Invite only people with whom you want to share this data. I cannot undo what people in
        your household change or delete; the app has no function for that. I do not mediate in
        disagreements within the household. My liability under Section&nbsp;10 and your
        statutory rights remain unaffected.
      </p>
      <p>
        The household is intended for private shared use, for example in a family or a shared
        flat. Business use, for instance in a café or for training courses, is not permitted.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Costs</h2>
      <p>
        Use is currently free of charge. If I introduce paid features later, separate terms
        will apply to them, to which you agree separately.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Test phase</h2>
      <p>
        BrewMind is in the test phase (TestFlight and closed testing on Google Play). The app is
        a test version: it may contain errors and is not continuously available. I can change
        features if there is a valid reason for doing so (for example security, bug fixing,
        technical development, feedback from the test) and you incur no costs as a result. If a
        change impairs your use more than merely insignificantly, I announce it beforehand in
        the notes on the new version (TestFlight or Google Play), and you can end the contract
        free of charge by deleting your account. Your statutory rights in the event of defects
        remain unaffected.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your content</h2>
      <p>
        What you enter in the app (for example names of beans and equipment, notes) remains
        yours. You grant me the right to store and process this content to the extent necessary
        for the account and the purposes described in the Privacy Policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are in a household with others, these people see your content, including your
        notes, and keep a copy when they leave the household. Do not enter anything there that
        the others should not read. You choose the name you give yourself for the household
        yourself; it must not deceive or insult anyone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Do not enter any content that infringes the rights of others or is unlawful.
      </p>

      <h2>8. What is not permitted</h2>
      <p>
        You may not disrupt, overload or circumvent the app and the service behind it, may not
        query it by automated means and may not attempt to access other people's data.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Termination and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        You can end the contract at any time without notice: in the app under „Verwaltung“
        (“Management”), „Konto“ (“Account”), „Konto löschen“ (“Delete account”) you delete your
        account. If you are alone in your household and have never shared it with others, all
        data backed up in it is thereby deleted; what otherwise remains is set out on the page
        about deletion. Your statutory right of withdrawal continues to exist alongside this.
        Details and the route without the app are set out on the page
        <a href="/loeschen/">Konto und Daten löschen</a> (in German).
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are in a household with others, deletion ends your account, not the household:
        the shared beans and equipment remain with the others, and for your shots you choose
        before deletion whether they are deleted as well or remain in the household without
        your name.
      </p>
      <p>
        I delete an account that has not been used for 24&nbsp;months, together with all data.
        If there are still other people in its household, I delete only the account; the shots
        remain in the household without a name.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the event of a serious breach of these terms, I can terminate the contract and block
        the account. I will tell you the reason and give you the opportunity to comment, insofar
        as I can reach you. Before deletion you can request a copy of your data. The same then
        applies to your shots in a household as with „Mitlöschen“ (“Delete as well”).
      </p>

      <h2>10. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        I am liable without limitation for intent, gross negligence and fraudulent intent, for
        injury to life, body or health, under a guarantee I have assumed and under the German
        Product Liability Act (Produkthaftungsgesetz). In the case of slight negligence I am
        liable only for the breach of essential contractual obligations and limited to the
        damage that is typically to be expected in contracts of this kind. Essential obligations
        are those whose fulfilment makes the contract possible in the first place and on whose
        observance you may regularly rely.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        I can change these terms in order to adapt them to new features, to changed laws or case
        law, or to requirements of the app stores. The new version is published on this page
        with a date. Changes that do not restrict your rights apply from publication on this
        page.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Law and dispute resolution</h2>
      <p>
        German law applies. If you are a consumer, the mandatory protective provisions of the
        state in which you have your habitual residence remain in place.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am neither willing nor obliged to take part in dispute resolution proceedings before a
        consumer arbitration board.
      </p>

      <p class="stand">Last updated: November 25, 2026</p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
